<title>POLAND: Stalexport wins toll highway concession.</title>
<headline>Stalexport wins toll highway concession.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Transport Ministry awarded Stalexport SA a concession to modernise and operate a 60 kilometre section of toll highway between the cities of Katowice and Krakow, Panorama television news programme said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said the government will cover the costs of modernising the road, which would become Poland's first toll highway, by the end of the year.</p>
<p>Passenger cars would pay between 3.0 and 3.5 U.S. cents per kilometre while trucks would pay at least twice that amount.</p>
<p>(( -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 ))</p>
